* @title A failed LOAD leaves the name undefined and is recoverable
* @attribution CSNOBOL4 test/loaderr.sno
* @nonstandard inline JS LOAD libraries are a snoflake extension
* @expect >>>
* QQQ1
* QQQ2
* <<<
* A library that will not compile fails the LOAD. The FUNCTION predicate
* then reports ZZZ undefined, so its OUTPUT is skipped, while a failed
* reload of QQQ leaves the working definition in place.
	LOAD("ZZZ()", "xyzzy")
	OUTPUT = FUNCTION(.ZZZ) "ZZZ"

	DEFINE("QQQ(X)")				:(EQQQ)
QQQ	QQQ = X						:(RETURN)
EQQQ

	OUTPUT = FUNCTION(.QQQ) QQQ("QQQ1")
	LOAD("QQQ()", "xyzzy")
	OUTPUT = FUNCTION(.QQQ) QQQ("QQQ2")
END
